               dh-sequence-python3,
               cmake,
               pkg-config,
               libgpiod-dev (>= 2.0)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: libadxl345-1
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: ADXL345 accelerometer library (runtime)
 A userspace driver for the ADXL345 over i2c-dev, with an opaque
 six-function C API, hidden visibility and a soname. It needs no kernel
 module: the part is driven entirely from user space.

Package: libadxl345-dev
Architecture: any
Section: libdevel
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libadxl345-1 (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: ADXL345 accelerometer library (development files)
 The header and the pkg-config file, so a third party links the library
 the way any library is linked.

Package: adxl345-tools
Architecture: any
# Four substitutions, and three of them were missing until lintian said
# so on Friday 2 October 2026, the first time this package was ever
# built. This stanza ships a compiled ELF (adxl-map), a python3 module
# (usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/adxl345) and a python3 script
# (adxl-motion), and declared a dependency on none of the three.
#
# shlibs:Depends  the C library adxl-map links against, libc included.
# python3:Depends the interpreter the module and the script need, filled
#                 by dh_python3 via the dh-sequence-python3 build
#                 dependency above.
#
# The Yocto recipe had the equivalent of the python one all along, and
# tests/adxl345-build-test.sh asserted it there. It asked one packaging
# system a question it never asked the other.
# adduser is a real dependency, not a formality. The postinst calls
# addgroup at line 12 and adduser at lines 25 and 30, both from the
# adduser package, and it runs under set -e. That package stopped being
# essential in Debian trixie, so on a minimal system the postinst dies,
# the package fails to configure and the service account is never
# created. That is criterion 5's own "the packages install cleanly"
# clause, and lintian found it as a WARNING, which this suite prints and
# does not score. It was read on Friday 2 October 2026 only because the
# suite had just been changed to print the warnings instead of counting
# them.
#
# Line 39 also says "adduser" and does not need this: it is an echo
# telling the admin what to type.
Depends: libadxl345-1 (>= ${source:Version}),
         adduser,
         ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${python3:Depends}
Description: ADXL345 reader and its udev rule
 adxl-map prints live acceleration. The package also ships the udev rule
 that puts /dev/i2c-* in group i2c, so that reading the sensor needs no
 root.
